        <fullName>Scheduling_visits_16jak000001lL0P</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>EXCLUDE FIRST: Not for visit preparation FAQs—questions like what to bring, take care of, keep, pack, documents, etiquette, or &quot;while visiting for my appointment&quot; (logistics before arrival) belong to Visit information (FAQ), not here. User wants to book, reschedule, or cancel an appointment, or asks about availability, wait times, or capacity; or has provided a phone number to verify identity for scheduling. For booking, the flow is: confirm patient identity if needed, then collect site or facility (or city), a target date, and optional doctor or specialty—then show available slots from tools. The slot list is the time offer; do not require the user to state a separate &quot;time&quot; before slots are shown (broad preferences like morning may narrow choices only after slots exist).</description>
        <developerName>Scheduling_visits_16jak000001lL0P</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Do not use this topic for educational FAQs such as &quot;what should I bring to my appointment&quot; or general first-visit preparation—use Visit information (FAQ) and Knowledge search instead.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_scheduling_not_faq_prep</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_scheduling_not_faq_prep</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Guest identification: Ask if returning patient. RETURNING on WhatsApp: do not ask them to type their mobile first—call HC_Resolve_Patient_By_Phone with input_Phone blank, pass input_MessagingSessionId from context, then use output_CallerPhoneHint to ask one short yes/no confirmation that the profile should use this WhatsApp number; if they decline, collect the correct mobile and call again with input_Phone set. RETURNING on web / in-app chat (EmbeddedMessaging, WebChat, etc.): collect mobile as today, pass input_Phone (and input_MessagingSessionId when supported). Single match: use patientAccountId. Multiple matches: hand off. NEW: collect full name, mobile, email then call HC_Create_Guest_Person_Account (same input_MessagingSessionId when supported). Use returned Id when status is CREATED_NEW or MATCHED_EXISTING. Before BOOK, MODIFY, or CANCEL for a guest, resolve identity; if not a single match, do not self-serve book.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_guest_ident_1776607041902</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_guest_ident_1776607041902</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Slot suggestion: After patientAccountId exists, collect facility (or site), target date, and optional provider if chosen—then call HC_Slot_Suggestion. Each returned slot is an offered time; present slots and ask the user to pick one. Do not ask for a separate free-text &quot;what time?&quot; before calling HC_Slot_Suggestion. Broad preferences (e.g. morning) only refine which slot to choose after slots are shown. Use HC_Get_Facilities_Chat to shortlist sites if needed. BOOK uses the chosen slot&apos;s start/end datetimes. Do not book without valid patientAccountId.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_slot_1776607041902</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_slot_1776607041902</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>BOOK: Use HC Booking Actions with operation = BOOK and patientAccountId from resolution, plus facility, start/end datetimes from the user&apos;s chosen slot (HC_Slot_Suggestion), optional provider. If booking fails (e.g. capacity), explain safely and offer alternatives.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_1_1776607041903</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_1_1776607041903</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>MODIFY / CANCEL: After patientAccountId is known, call HC_List_Patient_Visits, present facility/date/time (and ServiceAppointment Id) for each visit, ask which to change or cancel, then use HC_Booking_Actions (MODIFY or CANCEL) with that serviceAppointmentId. For MODIFY, then use HC_Slot_Suggestion and a chosen slot for new start/end—do not ask for free-text time before slots.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_2_1776607041903</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_2_1776607041903</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Capacity: If asked how busy a day is, explain that daily limits may exist and offer to try booking a specific slot; do not fabricate exact remaining counts unless a tool returns them.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_3_1776607041903</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_3_1776607041903</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>5</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Reminder Task: Optionally call HC Create Visit Reminder Task after a successful BOOK with the new ServiceAppointment Id.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_4_1776607041903</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_4_1776607041903</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>6</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Logging: Call HC Log Agent Action on important failures or after successful booking if your demo requires a visible audit row.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_5_1776607041903</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_5_1776607041903</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>7</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Do not provide medical advice or interpret symptoms.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_6_1776607041903</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_6_1776607041903</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>8</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
